Error: Jet.StrayCharacter: `\p` isn't an escape Jet knows
  --> Tests/UI/bad_escape.jet:2:14
    |
  2 |     print("C:\path")
    |              ^^
 Why: Inside quoted text, `\` starts an escape: `\n` (new line), `\r` (carriage return), `\t` (tab), `\"` (quote), `\\` (backslash), `\u{H}` (the Unicode scalar with hexadecimal value H)
 Fix: Write `\\` for a real backslash
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.StrayCharacter
